# (after 0524) nvn/memory (after 0512): idle re-upload spares retired after 3 s, uploaded textures idle 30 s freed at a memory-pressure trim and swept every 10 s on small devices, system memory in the logs
#
# Upstream:  https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/commit/d08d7da6239078a97f90ed71f0c27ec22c182eef  ("gfx/nvn: trim on memory pressure and evict idle spares and uploaded textures")
#            author seedds, 2026-11-23 01:57 +0800; Co-authored-by: Stan Bono
# Licence:   MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 seedds (nxnative LICENSE); ported from seedds/nxnative, MIT. The attribution above is kept as the licence asks.
#
# Why (measured upstream, Ocarina of Time on an 8 GB iPhone 17 across area transitions): 0.6-1.0 GB of Metal copies of uploaded textures of areas the player had left and up to 123 MB of
#   re-upload spares stayed resident; iOS sent memory-pressure warnings and ended the app for proc-thrashing at 67 MB free / 5.56 GB wired while os_proc_available_memory still read 2.7 GB.
#   Upstream result: 206 MB of old-area textures freed on the transition, frame time unchanged (iPhone 17); two trims 119 MB + 215 MB, residency set 3,487 -> 3,163 MB (16 GB M4).
# WHAT IT CHANGES (dm/gfx/nvn/nvn_mtl.m, hle_nvn.c, nvn_obj.h, nvn_owner.h, nvn_owner.m, dm/host/hle_hid.c; tests t_pkg_spare, t_pkg_evict, t_rt_recycle, t_hid, t_stick_deadzone):
#   - spare_trim: a packaged texture's spare (the texture its last re-upload replaced) waits at most 3 s (checked every 250 ms at a submission's start), then goes through defer_obj_release;
#   - pkg_evict_idle: an uploaded texture (NvPkg) that no texture ID used for 30 s (binds, shader pool reads: g_treg[].used, seen_stamp_used; resolutions outside pool walks: used_tu), not
#     sparse / placed / a view, never GPU-written and held by no pin, sharing entry or takeover, is let go with everything naming it (serial entries via own_drop_where_locked, its g_pkg_share
#     entry, views, view cache); its IDs are marked evicted and made again when a shader reads them or a bind needs them;
#   - pkg_sweep: on a device whose Metal working set is under 6 GB (8 GB iPhones, M1 iPads) the eviction also runs every 10 s without pressure. DM_NVN_TEX_EVICT_IDLE=0 / 1 forces it off / on;
#   - sys_mem: the system's free / wired / compressed / file-backed memory: a "system memory at frame" line after each memory report, in each trim's line, and one line per system
#     memory-pressure event; the memory report also prints when wired memory moved 256 MB or a pressure event or trim came;
#   - DM_CTL memtrim asks for a tier-1 trim (hle_hid.c);
#   - with the render-target release off (DM_NVN_RT_DEAD=0) the shaders' pool reads still stamp their IDs' use once a second.
# Merged into OUR 0512 (not upstream's mechanism): upstream adds its own DISPATCH_SOURCE_TYPE_MEMORYPRESSURE source and its mem_trim (DM_NVN_MEM_PRESSURE, warn on iOS / critical on the Mac).
#   Neither is taken: 0512's request (system source warn / critical, the app's request, the headroom watermark under 300 / 150 MB, DM_MEM_TRIM) stays the only trigger, and 0512's trim
#   (mem_trim_if_requested, at the next submission's start) now also frees every waiting render-target heap however fresh (rh_trim_all, was rh_trim under the policy), every spare
#   (spare_trim(1)) and the 30 s idle textures (pkg_evict_idle) before its GPU wait, so their releases drain in the same trim; its line says what each freed. DM_MEM_PRESSURE=0 still turns
#   the trim off; the 3 s spare retirement and the small-device sweep do not depend on it. 0512's own claim that re-upload spares are re-used on other threads does not hold on this tree
#   (tex_mtl_ re-uploads only on the submit thread, the others return the current texture), so they are trimmed here as upstream does. Upstream's view-cache delete by serial key is replaced by
#   a delete by the texture's address (this tree's g_vc key). t_rt_recycle's pressure case asks 0512's tier 2 instead of upstream's event; t_pkg_spare / t_pkg_evict likewise.
# Games: Ocarina of Time (8 GB iPhones) upstream; every game (spares, eviction on small devices, trims). Switches: DM_NVN_TEX_EVICT_IDLE (new); DM_MEM_PRESSURE, DM_MEM_TRIM, DM_MEM_HEADROOM (0512).
# Tests (M1 Pro): t_pkg_spare 59, t_pkg_evict 58, t_rt_recycle 60 + 60 + 2, t_mem_trim 18 + 7, t_rt_recycle_policy 57, t_session_reset, t_hid / t_stick_deadzone (host-unit); in HOST_TESTS.
# NOT measured here: wired memory, page-ins and DM_MEMSTAT on an iPhone; no real system pressure event was received on this Mac (the trims ran from DM_MEM_TRIM-style requests).
# Shader chain: not touched (b24b25240cad; scripts/build-host.sh checks it).
# Apply with: patch -p1, to the tree out-stage/out-engine/engine + engine-patches/0401..0524, in the order of the numbers of this folder (scripts/build-host.sh does).

